title: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> Planned Coup Discovered!
subtitle: Joshua Heath uncovers powerful evidence of a plot...
view-if: year == 1932 and month == 4 and not dufour_term_extended and marcher_heartland
priority: 4
tags: event
new-page: true
on-arrival: royalist_urgency += 1; interior_goal_heartland -= 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: sa_ban_braun if president_ideology == "Left"; sa_ban_normal if president_ideology != "Left"

= <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> Planned Coup Discovered!

@sa_ban_normal
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/sa_rally.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

With the presidential elections approaching[? if next_election_year_heartland == year:&nbsp;and the next Heartland elections as well?], Heartland Minister of the Interior Joshua Heath has ordered an emergency search of all <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> offices throughout the state.

During the raids, evidence was uncovered that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> Party headquarters in Avriza had ordered <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> units to be placed on high alert on election day. In the event of an anticipated [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] victory, these units were to immediately launch a coup d’état, which included the planned seizure of military installations and weaponry.

[? if president == "DuFour" and marcher_support_reactionary and dufour_run: The mere threat of such a coup has provided the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> with exactly what it needed to reenergize its reluctant membership in support of DuFour’s campaign against [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]?][? if president != "DuFour" or not marcher_support_reactionary or not dufour_run: The mere threat of such a coup has provided the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> with exactly what it needed to reenergize the workers against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>?]. Non-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> state governments broadly support banning the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, having lobbied the federal government for months on the issue. However, the more conservative, non-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> elements of the Commonwealth right, as well as the Commonwealth Army itself, do not share our sense of alarm over the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>’s supposed coup plans and see no need for immediate action.

- @sa_ban: We will use this revelation to commence a nationwide ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>!
- @sa_ban_pressure: We will leverage this revelation to pressure the Interior Ministry into banning the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> nationwide!
- @sa_ban_bruning: We will present this damning evidence to Interior Minister [? if second_bruning_cabinet_seen: Roland Ravabelle?][? if not second_bruning_cabinet_seen: Joseph Werth?] and push for a nationwide ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>!

@sa_ban
view-if: marcher_in_government and interior_minister_party == "Marcher"
on-arrival: loyalist_strength *= 0.65; loyalist_strength *= 0.7 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_militancy -= 0.1; loyalist_militancy -= 0.05 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned = 1; loyalist_nationwide_ban = 1; loyalist_banned_pro = 1 if (interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4; loyalist_banned_pro = 0 if (interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) < 1.4; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; interior_police_loyalty -= 0.05; loyalist_ban_timer = 6; loyalist_coup_progress = coup_progress; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 6; interior_goal_heartland -= 1; dufour_angry += 25; left_dissent -= 10; labor_dissent -= 5; disfavored_royalist -= 5; commons_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 3

With control of the Interior Ministry, we have used these revelations as a pretext to ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> nationwide[? if loyalist_banned:, as they can still operate outside of Heartland?]. This has led to a noticeable drop in political violence, effectively dealing a blow to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, who had relied on intimidation tactics to gain votes.

However, the ban has not been as effective as initially hoped. Few weapons have been seized, because the plans to ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Loyalists</span> were leaked by none other than General Kurt von Staal, who believes this move interferes with his "<span class="tooltip-text" title="Coined by conservative elites like Staal and Goodryke, this strategy aims to control the dynamic Royalist movement and integrate it into the state by introducing the party to government. In their eyes, this would moderate the Royalists, transforming them into a constructive component of the state.">taming strategy</span>." [? if president == "DuFour": He and the Commonwealth Army have submitted complaints to President DuFour, arguing that the accusations used to justify the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> ban equally apply to the Banners. The file presented to DuFour consists mostly of clippings from right-wing newspapers and a the Banners training manual. Even Ravabelle finds these charges groundless, but Staal wields significant influence over the aging president, who now believes that the ban must be extended to the Banners. ?]

[? if loyalist_banned_pro: Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> has been significantly weakened by the ban. ?]

@sa_ban_pressure
view-if: marcher_in_government and interior_minister_party != "Marcher"
on-arrival: loyalist_strength *= 0.7; loyalist_strength *= 0.7 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_militancy -= 0.1; loyalist_militancy -= 0.05 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned = 1; loyalist_nationwide_ban = 1; loyalist_banned_pro = 1 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned_pro = 0 if (interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) < 1.4; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; interior_police_loyalty -= 0.05; loyalist_ban_timer = 6; loyalist_coup_progress = coup_progress; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 6; interior_goal_heartland -= 1; dufour_angry += 20; left_dissent -= 10; labor_dissent -= 5; disfavored_royalist -= 5; commons_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 3

With our position in government, we pressure the Interior Ministry to ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> nationwide, for their anti-constitutional plot to overthrow the government. They quickly accede to these demands, banning the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> nationwide[? if loyalist_banned:, as they can still operate outside of Heartland?]. We have noticed a significant drop in political violence, and have dealt an effective blow to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, who have relied on their intimidation to gain votes.

However, the ban has not been as effective as initially hoped. Few weapons have been seized, because the plans to ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> were leaked by none other than General Kurt von Staal, who believes this move interferes with his "<span class="tooltip-text" title="Coined by conservative elites like Staal and Goodryke, this strategy aims to control the dynamic Royalist movement and integrate it into the state by introducing the party to government. In their eyes, this would moderate the Royalists, transforming them into a constructive component of the state.">taming strategy</span>." [? if president == "DuFour": He and the Commonwealth Army have submitted complaints to President DuFour, arguing that the accusations used to justify the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> ban equally apply to the Banners. The file presented to DuFour consists mostly of clippings from right-wing newspapers and a the Banners training manual. Even Ravabelle finds these charges groundless, but Staal wields significant influence over the aging president, who now believes that the ban must be extended to the Banners. ?]

[? if loyalist_banned_pro: Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> has been significantly weakened by the ban. ?]

