@sa_ban_bruning_groener
on-arrival: loyalist_strength *= 0.75; loyalist_strength *= 0.7 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_militancy -= 0.08; loyalist_militancy -= 0.05 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned = 1; loyalist_nationwide_ban = 1; loyalist_banned_pro = 1 if ((interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) >= 1.4) and not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned_pro = 0 if (interior_police_loyalty + heartland_police_loyalty) < 1.4; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; interior_police_loyalty -= 0.05; loyalist_ban_timer = 6; loyalist_coup_progress = coup_progress; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 6; interior_goal_heartland -= 1; dufour_angry_bruning += 20; groener_death = 1

Interior and Defense Minister Roland Ravabelle doesn't believe the findings to be urgent but concedes to the demands for a ban from nearly all state governments. As a result, an emergency decree has been issued, enforcing a nationwide ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, which all state governments are expected to enforce. We have already noticed a significant drop in political violence, and this decree has dealt a strong blow to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, who have relied on intimidation to gain votes.

However, the ban has not been as effective as initially hoped. Few weapons have been seized, because the plans to ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> were leaked by none other than General Kurt von Staal, who believes this move interferes with his "<span class="tooltip-text" title="Coined by conservative elites like Staal and Goodryke, this strategy aims to control the dynamic Royalist movement and integrate it into the state by introducing the party to government. In their eyes, this would moderate the Royalists, transforming them into a constructive component of the state.">taming strategy</span>." [? if president == "DuFour": He and the Commonwealth Army have submitted complaints to President DuFour, arguing that the accusations used to justify the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> ban equally apply to the Banners. The file presented to DuFour consists mostly of clippings from right-wing newspapers and a the Banners training manual. Even Ravabelle finds these charges groundless, but Staal wields significant influence over the aging president, who now believes that the ban must be extended to the Banners. ?]

[? if loyalist_banned_pro: Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> has been significantly weakened by the ban. ?]

