Interior Minister Joseph Werth, a strong anti-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> member of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s left wing, has found a strong urgency in our collected evidence to justify the ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>. As a result, an emergency decree has been issued, enforcing a nationwide ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, which all state governments are expected to enforce. We have already noticed a significant drop in political violence, and this decree has dealt a strong blow to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, who have relied on intimidation to gain votes.

